<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-SCA POSTS 35 PCT HIGHER H1 PROFIT.</title>
<headline>TABLE-SCA POSTS 35 PCT HIGHER H1 PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group SCA reported on Wednesday its earnings for the six months ending June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  2,253 vs  1,673</p>
<p> Sales					29,330 vs 28,214</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)				7.62  vs  5.03</p>
<p> Capital gain				 425  vs nil</p>
<p> Operating costs			  24,611 vs 24,303</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,961 vs  1,760</p>
<p> Associated interest			  14 vs     12</p>
<p> Operating profit			  2,772 vs  2,163</p>
<p> Net financial items	   CHARGE    519 vs    490 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     595 vs    552</p>
<p> Minorities				    153 vs    128</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,505 vs    993</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found SCA, full name Svenska Cellulosa Aktiebolaget, was expected to post a profit after financial items of 2.01 billion crowns including capital gains.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
